title: Example - Markdown link - reference style
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

CommonMark reference-style links separate the link TEXT from the link TARGET. A `[text][label]` usage refers to a `[label]: target "optional title"` definition. Lets you define a URL once at the top and reference it many times — clearer prose, easier maintenance.

''Single-pass limitation:'' definitions must appear BEFORE their usages in the source. Unresolved labels render as literal `[text][label]` characters. (CommonMark's full two-pass parse — where defs can appear anywhere — is deferred to a future revision.)

## Basic usage

[docs]: <Marker Fields>
[home]: https://tiddlywiki.com "TiddlyWiki home"

Live: see the [Marker Fields tiddler][docs] for full marker config, or visit [TiddlyWiki's homepage][home].

Source:

```
[docs]: <Marker Fields>
[home]: https://tiddlywiki.com "TiddlyWiki home"

see the [Marker Fields tiddler][docs] for full marker config, or visit [TiddlyWiki's homepage][home].
```

The definitions sit on their own lines (invisible in the rendered output). Each `[...][label]` usage looks the label up in the per-parser ref store and substitutes the def's target. The `home` def's `"TiddlyWiki home"` title becomes the link's `tooltip` attribute.

## Same label, different text

[mfields]: <Marker Fields>

Live: read [the field reference][mfields], or [the same place again][mfields], or [yet another link to it][mfields].

Source:

```
[mfields]: <Marker Fields>

read [the field reference][mfields], or [the same place again][mfields], or [yet another link to it][mfields].
```

One def, many references — the maintenance pattern reference-style links are designed for.

## Labels are case-insensitive and whitespace-normalized

[Click Me]: <Marker Kinds>

Live: [the kinds doc][CLICK ME] / [same place][click   me] / [also same][  Click   Me  ]

Source:

```
[Click Me]: <Marker Kinds>

[the kinds doc][CLICK ME] / [same place][click   me] / [also same][  Click   Me  ]
```

All three label-references resolve to the same def (CommonMark normalization: lowercase, whitespace collapsed, trimmed).

## Unresolved label falls through

Live: [this label doesn't exist][nonexistent-label] — renders as literal characters.

Source:

```
[this label doesn't exist][nonexistent-label]
```

No def, no link — the raw `[...][...]` text shows through.

